199ea00e","id":"F001","line":246,"path":"agentic_preflight/reviewers/orchestration.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Record a list of (phase, digest) entries with duplicates removed, or document that the report keeps only the last prompt per phase. Then check this against the eight-prompt limit enforced in review_executor.","title":"Prompt digests are keyed by phase, so a phase called more than once reports only its last prompt","unit":"U0013"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"`_REPORT_PROMPT_LIMIT = 8` rejects the whole report when `prompts` has more than eight entries. Nothing logs this or tells the agent. If the packaged orchestrator can produce more than eight phases (with verify and retries), no `reviewer_reported` event is written for a real review, and no one can tell why.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F002","line":70,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/review_executor.py","response_note":"Resolved by repair commit 8f77c8a2, the same commit that fixed F001: review run now appends a reviewer_report_ignored event with the reason when it drops a report, and the packaged reviewer reports at most one entry per distinct phase and prompt, far below the limit of eight. In-place mode accepts one fixed response per new commit, so this finding cites the commit here.","severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"dismissed","suggestion":"Make sure the limit is above the largest number of phases the orchestrator can produce, or record why a report was rejected.","title":"A report with more than eight prompts is dropped whole without notice","unit":"U0028"},{"action":"no_op","code_owned":false,"detail":"The event is written before `submit_findings`. A review whose submission is later rejected as `InvalidFindings` still leaves a `reviewer_reported` event, as if the review had completed. This is acceptable if the event only records what the command printed, but readers of the log should know it.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F003","line":237,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/review_executor.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"open","suggestion":null,"title":"reviewer_reported is appended before the submission is validated","unit":"U0029"},{"action":"no_op","code_owned":false,"detail":"The report is read from the redacted output. `_REPORT_NAME` allows `[` and `]`, so a value that was replaced with `[redacted]` passes the check and is recorded as the model or provider name. It leaks nothing, but the event then holds a placeholder instead of a real name.","fix_commit":null,"id":"F004","line":36,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/review_executor.py","response_note":null,"severity":"low","stage":"review","status":"open","suggestion":null,"title":"The name pattern accepts redaction markers such as \"[redacted]\"","unit":"U0028"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"Orchestrator.note_prompt records one entry for each distinct (phase, prompt) pair, so every discovery chunk and every verification prompt adds an entry. A review with a large diff, or with several findings to verify, can easily send more than 8 distinct prompts. When that happens, _checked_report rejects the whole report with too_many_prompts and records reviewer_report_ignored instead of reviewer_reported. The intent says the packaged reviewer reports provider, model, effort and prompt digests, but a reviewer working as designed would fail that check. The tests only cover reviews with one to three prompts.","fix_commit":"06641f066da4ef359c3558933b7b2f36a69897f4","id":"F005","line":39,"path":"agentic_preflight/runs/review_executor.py","response_note":null,"severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Choose one: raise or remove _REPORT_PROMPT_LIMIT and bound the report by total size instead; have the orchestrator group digests by phase or cap them itself; or document that large reviews record reviewer_report_ignored. Add a test where the orchestrator sends more than 8 prompts.","title":"Packaged reviewer's own report is dropped as too_many_prompts on multi-prompt reviews","unit":"U0028"},{"action":"ask_user","code_owned":false,"detail":"chain_status returns 'unchained' (not 'broken') whenever no line carries CHAIN_KEY. That lets old-release logs pass, but it means a run this release created can be downgraded on purpose. Remove prev_sha256 from every line of events.jsonl, then edit, delete or reorder lines freely, and verify_events reports 'unchained' with no breaks. require_event_chain only refuses 'broken', so mergeback goes on to attest the edited history. Deleting events.jsonl entirely gives 'empty' and also passes. So the intent that mergeback refuse an edited, removed or inserted line only holds while at least one chained line is left.","fix_commit":"21e5f5f9fec1edd8291e34736f130a818dc9b39d","id":"F006","line":256,"path":"agentic_preflight/store.py","response_note":null,"severity":"medium","stage":"review","status":"fixed","suggestion":"Record in the run document that this release started the run, or the line where chaining began (run schema 2 must stay unchanged, so this may need a field that already exists or a marker kept outside the log). Then treat 'unchained' or 'empty' as broken for any run that should be chained. If that is out of scope, document the downgrade alongside the removed-tail limitation.","title":"A fully chained log can be made to pass by removing prev_sha256 from every line","unit":"U0032"}],"fingerprint":{"base_tree_sha":"627ae6b209ab6133ba755218b2b06f3d2bad9eca","config_sha256":"25363ddc7d586ecf84e8f7f7fa372aa5c9e7aa56e8216e0ac04452b84d670e9c","configuration_supported":true,"diff_sha256":"9d2ea929e98b6de1f8fd4dd6ef4c9aa15d1ce725aa3b92a27858e8bb9b71b8bf","excluded_files":[],"executor":"command","grounding_sha256":"3c8e2d59b25d34071e8554b2e200d742cee9febb44f354f2e3c91dc9f1ab3a71","head_tree_sha":"73aac8c18e3e29cc13a30ae4e58ee26c1901c663","intent_sha256":"91c3bd23085dc0a794a0993f10006095994c69702da2dae